#message 30 "You don't have a report."
#message 31 "Walk up to the front desk first."
#message 32 "You drop the report in the red tray. Prakash fishes it out without looking up. \"That's the WRONG TRAY, Reyes. It says so on the tray. Hand it to me.\""
#message 33 "Prakash reads the report once for the facts and once for the spelling."
#message 34 "Prakash: \"Timeline from the manifest. Photographs and a bottle from Hollis. The lease on Warehouse 9. An arrest with backup on scene.\" He stamps the report. \"That'll stick. Good work, Reyes.\""
#message 35 "He drops the report in the IN tray. Your first case is closed and your first shift is over. Bud Bukowski owes you a coffee, and he is already telling everyone how it went."
#message 36 "Prakash reads the report and hands it back. \"It's got holes, Reyes.\""
#message 37 "Prakash: \"Kowal's statement hasn't been checked against anything.\""
#message 38 "Prakash: \"No photographs or physical evidence from the pharmacy.\""
#message 39 "Prakash: \"Nothing ties this to a location. Where did the stock go?\""
